  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the 10 files that establish the full error-provenance chain:\n\n**Netty (channel pipeline exception handling):**\n- `DefaultChannelPipeline.java` \u2014 pipeline's `fireExceptionCaught`, default tail handler behavior (logs and drops unhandled exceptions)\n- `AbstractChannelHandlerContext.java` \u2014 per-handler exception propagation mechanics\n- `ChannelPipeline.java` \u2014 inbound/outbound event contract, `fireExceptionCaught` propagation model\n- `ChannelInboundHandlerAdapter.java` \u2014 default `exceptionCaught` forwards to next handler (where custom handlers often fail to override and lose context)\n\n**Spring WebFlux (reactor-netty bridge \u2192 WebFlux error handling):**\n- `ReactorHttpHandlerAdapter.java` \u2014 the actual Netty\u2194reactor-netty\u2194WebFlux bridge point; wraps `HttpServerRequest`/`HttpServerResponse` and only catches `URISyntaxException` explicitly, letting other exceptions flow into the reactive chain as generic `Throwable`\n- `ReactorServerHttpResponse.java` \u2014 adapts `ServerHttpResponse` onto reactor-netty's response, where Netty-level write failures surface\n- `AbstractServerHttpResponse.java` \u2014 base commit/write logic shared across adapters\n- `HttpWebHandlerAdapter.java` \u2014 `handleUnresolvedError`, where any uncaught exception becomes a generic 500 (`isDisconnectedClientError` heuristically strings-matches \"connection reset by peer\"/\"broken pipe\" instead of using typed Netty exceptions)\n- `ExceptionHandlingWebHandler.java` \u2014 the exception handler chain that runs before `HttpWebHandlerAdapter`'s catch-all\n- `ResponseStatusExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 only understands `ResponseStatusException`; any other exception type (including anything originating from Netty) falls through to the generic path\n\nThe error-context loss happens at the `ReactorHttpHandlerAdapter`/`HttpWebHandlerAdapter` boundary: Netty channel exceptions arrive as opaque `Throwable`s with no structured type info, and `isDisconnectedClientError` falls back to lowercase substring matching on the exception message rather than checking Netty-specific exception types, which is where provenance (which handler, which pipeline stage) is discarded in favor of a flat 500.",
